---
import Window from "../Window.astro";
---

<Window
  title="RetroFinder Manual"
  id="window-manual"
  windowId="manual"
  class="w-full max-w-md"
  footer="Page 1 of 1"
>
  <div
    class="p-4 font-body text-body-lg leading-relaxed overflow-y-auto"
    style="max-height: 320px;"
  >
    <p class="font-mono text-label-lg font-bold mb-3">
      RETROFINDER 1.0 USER GUIDE
    </p>

    <p class="mb-3">
      Welcome to RetroFinder, your gateway to the history of personal computing.
    </p>

    <p class="font-mono text-label-sm opacity-70 mb-1">OPENING APPLICATIONS</p>
    <p class="mb-3">
      Click any icon on the right side of the desktop to open its corresponding
      window. Each application will load from disk — please wait for the cursor
      to return to normal.
    </p>

    <p class="font-mono text-label-sm opacity-70 mb-1">MOVING WINDOWS</p>
    <p class="mb-3">
      Click and drag the title bar of any window to reposition it on the
      desktop. An outline will indicate the new position before you release.
    </p>

    <p class="font-mono text-label-sm opacity-70 mb-1">CLOSING WINDOWS</p>
    <p class="mb-3">
      Click the small square on the left of the title bar to close a
      window.
    </p>

    <p class="font-mono text-label-sm opacity-70 mb-1">MINIMIZING WINDOWS</p>
    <p class="mb-3">
      Click the striped button on the right of the title bar to minimize a
      window. Double-click the minimized title bar or click again to restore it.
    </p>

    <p class="font-mono text-label-sm opacity-70 mb-1">TERMINAL</p>
    <p class="mb-3">
      Open the Terminal and type HELP for a list of available commands. Type
      EXIT to close the terminal.
    </p>

    <p class="font-mono text-label-sm opacity-70 mb-1">KEYBOARD SHORTCUT</p>
    <p>Clicking Desktop in the menu bar minimizes all open windows.</p>
  </div>
</Window>
